        "source": "youtube.com",
        "publisher": "NASA",
        "title": "U.S. Spacewalk 96",
        "description": "At approximately 8:35 a.m. EDT (1235 UTC) on Aug. 6, 2026, NASA astronauts Anil Menon and Jessica Meir will venture outside the International Space Station for an approximately six-and-a-half-hour spacewalk. The pair will install hardware that will modify the station’s 3B power channel and prepare it for the future installation of an International Space Station Roll-Out Solar Array.\n\nThis spacewalk will be the first for Menon and the sixth for Meir. Meir will serve as spacewalk crew member 1 and will wear a suit with red stripes. Menon will serve as crew member 2 and will wear an unmarked suit.\n\nLearn more about this spacewalk: https://go.nasa.gov/4x9ASdi\nRead the latest mission updates from the station: https://nasa.gov/blogs/spacestation/\n\nCredit: NASA",
